{
  "item": "U10",
  "name": "CAP-U10STEPPREDICT",
  "question": "Rule P's step on other Layouts lists, predicted before the read: h1p1 (heading, paragraph), p1i1 (paragraph, image) and Instagram, each through one walk that has every layout right after every other once.",
  "rules": {
    "S": "A content-fit block (Text, Instagram) takes its low span right after the list's tallest-box layouts for that block, and its high span after anything else. The tallest layouts themselves take the low span right after a layout where the block's box is centred (start line + end line = 28) with other areas. A block whose boxes are all one height has no step; images, like Flickr, have none. Boxes from the probe-word reads (CAP-U10ALIGN-B.json, CAP-U10ALIGN-D.json, CAP-U10FADED-A.json). Fitted on p1 (CAP-U10ROWS-A.json) and Instagram (CAP-U10FADED-A.json, CAP-U10SHARE-INSTAGRAM.json): seen."
  },
  "scoring": "Per pick and block, the desktop span (end line - start line). same: the span equals the one the layout shows most often in the walk. high: equals the most common span among this layout's high-predicted reads. low: less than that. The first pick of each walk (after the start) is not scored.",
